 eosinophils as the three granulocytes."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Agranulocytes","clue":"Agranulocytes = lymphocytes and monocytes","detail":"These are the two white-cell types with very small, hard-to-see granules."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Neutrophil","clue":"Neutrophils are common first phagocytes","detail":"They are the most common white cells and engulf microorganisms."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Basophil","clue":"Basophils release histamine and heparin","detail":"Histamine promotes inflammation; heparin helps prevent clot formation."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Eosinophil","clue":"Eosinophils = allergy and worms","detail":"They participate in allergic responses and help destroy certain parasitic worms."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Lymphocyte","clue":"Lymphocytes = antibody and immune responses","detail":"Lymphocytes include cells involved in antibody production and other immune functions."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Monocyte","clue":"Monocytes move into tissues and become macrophages","detail":"Macrophages phagocytize debris and can present processed foreign material to lymphocytes."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Platelet plug","clue":"Platelet plug = quick patch for a small break","detail":"Platelets accumulate at minor vessel damage to help seal it."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Prothrombinase","clue":"Prothrombinase activates prothrombin","detail":"It converts prothrombin into thrombin in the clotting sequence."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Thrombin","clue":"Thrombin turns fibrinogen into fibrin","detail":"Fibrin strands then form a mesh that stabilizes the clot."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Antithrombin","clue":"Antithrombin and heparin limit clotting","detail":"These anticoagulants help prevent unwanted clot formation."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Fibrinolysis","clue":"Fibrinolysis = breaking down fibrin clots","detail":"Plasmin carries out clot breakdown."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Type A blood","clue":"A type = A antigen, anti-B antibody","detail":"Type A red cells carry A antigen; plasma has anti-B antibodies."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Type AB blood","clue":"AB type = both antigens, neither antibody","detail":"Type AB red cells have A and B antigens; plasma has neither anti-A nor anti-B."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Type O blood","clue":"O type = no A/B antigens, both antibodies","detail":"Type O red cells have neither antigen, while plasma has anti-A and anti-B."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"ABO antigens","clue":"ABO type is written on the red-cell surface","detail":"The presence or absence of A and B antigens determines the ABO group."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Crossmatch","clue":"Crossmatch = test donor against recipient","detail":"The test checks whether donor and recipient blood agglutinate."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Complete blood count (CBC)","clue":"CBC = RBC, hemoglobin, hematocrit, WBC","detail":"These are the core measurements listed for a CBC in the chapter."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Differential white blood count","clue":"Differential = proportions of five white-cell types","detail":"It reports the percentages of neutrophils, lymphocytes, monocytes, eosinophils, and basophils."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Leukocytosis","clue":"Leukocytosis = high white-cell count","detail":"Bacterial infection commonly raises the neutrophil count."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Thrombocytopenia","clue":"Thrombocytopenia = too few platelets","detail":"A greatly reduced platelet count can cause bleeding through small vessels."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Prothrombin time","clue":"PT/INR = time for clotting to start","detail":"The INR standardizes prothrombin-time results across different thromboplastin reagents."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Transport of respiratory gases","clue":"Blood carries oxygen out and carbon dioxide back","detail":"Oxygen travels from lungs to cells; carbon dioxide travels from tissues to lungs."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Clotting","clue":"Clotting sequence: factors → prothrombinase → thrombin → fibrin","detail":"Fibrin forms the threadlike network that stabilizes a clot."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"ABO blood group","clue":"ABO group follows A and B red-cell antigens","detail":"The chapter describes A, B, AB, and O by antigen and plasma-antibody patterns."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"ABO blood groups","clue":"Mismatch can make red cells agglutinate or lyse","detail":"Antibodies binding incompatible red-cell antigens can cause a transfusion reaction."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular & Blood","term":"Plasma osmotic composition","clue":"Plasma solutes help maintain fluid and ion balance","detail":"Blood buffers help regulate pH, while osmotic composition supports fluid balance."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular System","term":"Tricuspid valve","clue":"Tricuspid = right atrium to right ventricle","detail":"The right atrioventricular valve guards flow into the right ventricle."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular System","term":"Pulmonary valve","clue":"Pulmonary = right ventricular exit to the lungs","detail":"The pulmonary semilunar valve opens from the right ventricle into the pulmonary trunk."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular System","term":"Mitral valve","clue":"Mitral / bicuspid = left atrium to left ventricle","detail":"The mitral valve is the left atrioventricular valve."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular System","term":"Aortic valve","clue":"Aortic = left ventricular exit to the body","detail":"The aortic semilunar valve opens from the left ventricle into the aorta."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular System","term":"Atrioventricular valves","clue":"AV valves = tricuspid and mitral","detail":"They sit between the atria and ventricles and close during ventricular contraction."},{"topic":"Cardiovascular System","term":"Semilunar valves","clue":"Semilunar = pulmonary and aortic","detail":"They guard the two ventricular exits into the pulmonary trunk and aorta."}];let state={xp:0,streak:0,correct:0,answered:0,sessionCorrect:0,sessionAnswered:0,topicStats:{}};
let pool=[],index=0,runTopic='ALL',runSize=20,missed=[];
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);
function shuffle(a){for(let i=a.length-1;i>0;i--){const j=Math.floor(Math.random()*(i+1));[a[i],a[j]]=[a[j],a[i]]}return a}
function esc(s){return String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,m=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[m]))}
function save(){localStorage.setItem('nurseCoreX',JSON.stringify(state))}
function load(){try{const x=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('nurseCoreX'));if(x)state={...state,...x};state.topicStats=state.topicStats||{}}catch(e){state.topicStats={}}}
function hud(){}
function shell(inner){return `<div class="shell">${inner}</div>`}
function home(){hud();$('screen').innerHTML=shell(`<section class="hero"><div><div class="eyebrow"><i class="dot"></i> NURSING REVIEW READY</div><h1>MASTER THE<br><span>HUMAN BODY.</span></h1><p></p><div class="cards"><div class="mini"><b>${BANK.length}</b><span>QUESTIONS</span></div><div class="mini"><b>${TOPICS.length}</b><span>TOPIC AREAS</span></div><div class="mini"><b>100%</b><span>SHUFFLED</span></div><div class="mini"><b>EXPLAINED</b><span>FEEDBACK</span></div></div><div class="controls"><button class="primary" onclick="setup()">ENTER CLINICAL RUN</button><button class="ghost" onclick="topicsPage()">CURRICULUM</button><button class="ghost" onclick="cluesPage()">KEYWORD CLUES</button><button class="ghost" onclick="progressPage()">TOPIC PROGRESS</button><button class="ghost" onclick="manual()">STUDY GUIDE</button></div></div><div class="hero-art"><div class="scan"></div><div class="orb"></div></div></section>`)}
function setup(){hud();$('screen').innerHTML=shell(`<section class="setup"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">PICK WHAT TO STUDY</div><h2>Choose your topic</h2><p class="muted">Focus on one area, or mix questions from the full curriculum.</p></div><div class="muted">${BANK.length} questions across ${TOPICS.length} topics</div></div><div class="formgrid"><label>TOPIC TO TACKLE<select id="topicSel" onchange="updateTopicCount()"><option value="ALL">All topics — mixed review (${BANK.length} questions)</option>${TOPICS.map(t=>`<option value="${esc(t)}">${esc(t)} — ${BANK.filter(q=>q.topic===t).length} questions</option>`).join('')}</select><span id="topicCount" class="muted">Questions will be drawn across every topic.</span></label><label>HOW MANY QUESTIONS?<select id="sizeSel"><option value="10">10 — Quick drill</option><option value="20" selected>20 — Focus session</option><option value="40">40 — Deep review</option><option value="80">80 — Extended review</option><option value="100">100 — Exam set</option><option value="150">150 — Long session</option><option value="170">170 — Extended session</option><option value="200">200 — Long review</option><option value="ALL">All available questions</option></select></label></div><div class="controls"><button onclick="home()">BACK</button><button class="primary" onclick="start()">START REVIEW →</button></div></section>`);updateTopicCount()}
function updateTopicCount(){const sel=$('topicSel'),out=$('topicCount');if(!sel||!out)return;const topic=sel.value,n=topic==='ALL'?BANK.length:BANK.filter(q=>q.topic===topic).length;out.textContent=topic==='ALL'?`Questions will be drawn across all ${TOPICS.length} topics (${n} total).`:`${n} questions available in ${topic}.`;const size=$('sizeSel');if(size)for(const option of size.options)option.disabled=option.value!=='ALL'&&+option.value>n;}function start(){runTopic=$('topicSel').value;let source=runTopic==='ALL'?[...BANK]:BANK.filter(q=>q.topic===runTopic);runSize=$('sizeSel').value==='ALL'?source.length:+$('sizeSel').value;pool=shuffle([...source]).slice(0,Math.min(runSize,source.length));index=0;missed=[];state.sessionCorrect=0;state.sessionAnswered=0;renderQ()}function renderQ(){hud();let q=pool[index];let choices=q.choices.map((text,i)=>({text,exp:q.explanations[i],correct:i===q.answer}));if(choices.length<4){const used=new Set(q.choices.map(x=>x.toLowerCase()));const poolChoices=BANK.filter(item=>item.topic===q.topic&&item!==q).flatMap(item=>item.choices.filter((_,i)=>i!==item.answer)).filter(text=>!used.has(text.toLowerCase()));const extra=shuffle(poolChoices)[0]||'None of the above';choices.push({text:extra,exp:'This is a related option, but it does not answer this question. Review the explanation for the correct choice.',correct:false})}shuffle(choices);q._choices=choices;const pct=Math.round(index/pool.length*100);$('screen').innerHTML=shell(`<div class="quiz"><aside class="side"><div class="eyebrow">TOPIC MAP</div><h3>ACTIVE TOPICS</h3><div class="topiclist">${TOPICS.map(t=>`<div class="topic ${t===q.topic?'active':''}">${esc(t)}</div>`).join('')}</div><div class="progress"><div class="muted">REVIEW PROGRESS</div><div class="bar"><i style="width:${pct}%"></i></div><div class="muted" style="font-size:10px;margin-top:7px">${index+1} / ${pool.length}</div></div><button class="ghost progress-shortcut" onclick="progressPage()">VIEW TOPIC PROGRESS</button></aside><section class="qmain"><div class="qmeta"><span class="tag">${esc(q.topic)}</span><span class="qnum">QUESTION ${index+1} • ${pool.length}</span></div><div class="question">${esc(q.q)}</div><div class="choices">${choices.map((c,i)=>`<button class="choice" onclick="answer(${i})"><span class="letter">${'ABCD'[i]}</span><span>${esc(c.text)}</span></button>`).join('')}</div><div id="feedback" class="feedback"></div></section></div>`)}function answer(i){const buttons=[...document.querySelectorAll('.choice')];if(buttons.some(b=>b.classList.contains('locked')))return;const q=pool[index],choices=q._choices,good=choices.findIndex(c=>c.correct);buttons.forEach((b,n)=>{b.classList.add('locked');if(n===good)b.classList.add('correct');if(n===i&&i!==good)b.classList.add('wrong')});state.answered++;state.sessionAnswered++;state.topicStats=state.topicStats||{};const topicStat=state.topicStats[q.topic]||(state.topicStats[q.topic]={answered:0,correct:0});topicStat.answered++;if(i===good){state.correct++;state.sessionCorrect++;topicStat.correct++;state.streak++}else{state.streak=0;missed.push({q,selected:choices[i].text,correct:choices[good].text})}save();hud();const chosen=choices[i],right=choices[good];$('feedback').innerHTML=`<div class="explain ${i===good?'good':'bad'}"><b>${i===good?'✓ CORRECT — CORRECT — KNOWLEDGE CONFIRMED':'✕ REVIEW — CORRECT ANSWER'}</b><p><b>Your choice:</b> ${esc(chosen.text)}</p><p>${esc(chosen.exp)}</p>${i!==good?`<p><b>Why the correct answer works:</b> ${esc(right.exp)}</p>`:''}</div><div class="nextrow"><button class="primary" onclick="next()">${index+1===pool.length?'VIEW RESULTS':'NEXT QUESTION →'}</button></div>`}
function next(){index++;if(index>=pool.length)finish();else renderQ()}
function finish(){hud();const pct=Math.round(state.sessionCorrect/state.sessionAnswered*100);$('screen').innerHTML=shell(`<section class="result"><div class="eyebrow">REVIEW COMPLETE</div><h2>REVIEW RESULTS</h2><div class="score">${pct}%</div><p>${state.sessionCorrect} / ${state.sessionAnswered} correct</p><div class="cards"><div class="mini"><b>${state.sessionCorrect}</b><span>CORRECT</span></div><div class="mini"><b>${state.sessionAnswered-state.sessionCorrect}</b><span>TO REVIEW</span></div><div class="mini"><b>${state.sessionAnswered}</b><span>QUESTIONS DONE</span></div><div class="mini"><b>${missed.length}</b><span>REVIEW ITEMS</span></div></div>${missed.length?`<div class="review">${missed.slice(0,12).map(m=>`<div class="explain bad"><b>${esc(m.q.topic)}</b><p>${esc(m.q.q)}</p><span class="muted">Correct: ${esc(m.correct)}</span></div>`).join('')}</div>`:`<h3 style="color:var(--mint);margin-top:35px">PERFECT RUN — GREAT WORK</h3>`}<div class="controls" style="justify-content:center">${missed.length?`<button onclick="retryMissed()">RETRY MISSED (${missed.length})</button>`:''}<button onclick="setup()">NEW RUN</button><button class="primary" onclick="home()">NURSING REVIEW</button></div></section>`)}
function retryMissed(){pool=shuffle(missed.map(m=>m.q));index=0;missed=[];runSize=pool.length;state.sessionCorrect=0;state.sessionAnswered=0;renderQ()}
function progressPage(){const stats=state.topicStats||{};const cards=TOPICS.map(t=>{const x=stats[t]||{answered:0,correct:0},pct=x.answered?Math.round(x.correct/x.answered*100):0,status=!x.answered?'Not started':x.answered<5?'Building':pct<70?'Review needed':pct<85?'Building':'Strong';return `<article class="topic-progress-card"><div class="topic-progress-head"><b>${esc(t)}</b><span class="progress-status ${status==='Review needed'?'needs-review':status==='Strong'?'strong':''}">${status}</span></div><div class="bar"><i style="width:${pct}%"></i></div><div class="muted progress-detail">${x.answered?`${pct}% accuracy · ${x.correct} / ${x.answered} correct`:'No questions answered yet'}</div><button class="ghost" onclick="setupTopic('${esc(t)}')">PRACTICE THIS TOPIC</button></article>`}).join('');$('screen').innerHTML=shell(`<section class="topics-page progress-page"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">YOUR STUDY HISTORY</div><h2>Topic progress</h2><p class="muted">Results are saved in this browser and updated as you answer.</p></div></div><div class="progress-grid">${cards}</div><div class="controls"><button onclick="home()">BACK TO HOME</button><button class="primary" onclick="setup()">START A REVIEW</button></div></section>`)}
function setupTopic(topic){setup();$('topicSel').value=topic;updateTopicCount()}function topicsPage(){$('screen').innerHTML=shell(`<section class="topics-page"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">MASTER CURRICULUM</div><h2>Complete A&P Review</h2></div></div><div class="topicgrid">${TOPICS.map(t=>`<div class="topiccard"><b>${esc(t)}</b><span class="muted">${BANK.filter(q=>q.topic===t).length} questions</span></div>`).join('')}</div><div class="controls"><button class="primary" onclick="setup()">START THIS CURRICULUM</button><button onclick="home()">BACK</button></div></section>`)}
function cluesPage(){const cards=items=>items.map(c=>`<article class="clue-card"><div class="clue-top"><span class="tag">${esc(c.topic)}</span></div><h3>${esc(c.term)}</h3><p class="clue-memory">${esc(c.clue)}</p><p class="muted">${esc(c.detail)}</p></article>`).join('');$('screen').innerHTML=shell(`<section class="topics-page clues-page"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">FAST MEMORY CUES</div><h2>Keyword clues</h2><p class="muted">Spot a term in a question and connect it to the fact it points to.</p></div><div class="clue-total">${KEYWORD_CLUES.length} quick clues</div></div><label class="clue-search-label">FIND A TERM OR CLUE<input id="clueSearch" type="search" placeholder="Try: tunica, afferent, insulin, water" oninput="filterClues()"></label><div id="clueResults" class="clue-grid">${cards(KEYWORD_CLUES)}</div><p id="clueEmpty" class="muted" hidden>No matching clue yet. Try a different word.</p><div class="controls"><button onclick="home()">BACK TO HOME</button><button class="primary" onclick="setup()">START A REVIEW</button></div><p class="muted clue-note">Memory cues are study aids. Read the explanation and use your course materials for full context.</p></section>`)}
function filterClues(){const query=$('clueSearch').value.toLowerCase().trim();const matches=KEYWORD_CLUES.filter(c=>(c.topic+' '+c.term+' '+c.clue+' '+c.detail).toLowerCase().includes(query));$('clueResults').innerHTML=matches.map(c=>`<article class="clue-card"><div class="clue-top"><span class="tag">${esc(c.topic)}</span></div><h3>${esc(c.term)}</h3><p class="clue-memory">${esc(c.clue)}</p><p class="muted">${esc(c.detail)}</p></article>`).join('');$('clueEmpty').hidden=matches.length>0;}function manual(){$('screen').innerHTML=shell(`<section class="manual"><div class="eyebrow">STUDY GUIDE</div><h2>How the nursing study game works</h2><p><b>1.</b> Choose any topic or the complete curriculum.</p><p><b>2.</b> Choose a question count or practice every available question in the selected pool.</p><p><b>3.</b> Every case is shuffled, and the three answer choices are independently shuffled on every question.</p><p><b>4.</b> After you answer, the game immediately shows the selected choice explanation and, when needed, why the correct answer is correct.</p><p><b>5.</b> Correct answers are highlighted immediately. Wrong answers go into the run's review list.</p><p><b>6.</b> The midterm question bank covers the original Muscle, Bone, Cardiovascular/Blood, and Nervous questions plus Cell Biology, Histology, Integumentary, Special Senses, Endocrine, Respiratory, Digestive, Urinary, Reproductive, Lymphatic/Immune, Homeostasis, Fluids/Electrolytes, Metabolism/Nutrition, Genetics, Acid-Base, Anatomical Terminology, and Nursing Clinical A&P.</p><p class="muted">Educational practice only. Use your school's modules, instructor guidance, and approved references for your actual nursing curriculum.</p><div class="controls"><button class="primary" onclick="home()">RETURN TO NURSING REVIEW</button></div></section>`)}
load();home();
</script></body></html>
